WEBVTT

1
00:02:24.041 --> 00:02:27.875
In the previous twenty-three
verses of Chapter 11,

2
00:02:27.875 --> 00:02:30.666
Arjun, beholding Lord Krishna's Vishwarupa,

3
00:02:30.666 --> 00:02:33.416
began describing it.

4
00:02:33.416 --> 00:02:34.791
In the coming verses, Arjun

5
00:02:34.791 --> 00:02:37.916
expands this description further.

6
00:02:37.916 --> 00:02:41.125
As Arjun beholds the Vishwarupa,

7
00:02:41.125 --> 00:02:43.083
his initial wonder

8
00:02:43.083 --> 00:02:45.625
deepens into profound fear.

9
00:02:45.625 --> 00:02:47.333
He sees Lord Krishna's vast,

10
00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.291
radiant form

11
00:02:49.291 --> 00:02:52.500
reaching to the sky, with blazing

12
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.916
eyes and enormous, terrifying mouths.

13
00:02:55.916 --> 00:02:57.625
This sight is so overwhelming

14
00:02:57.625 --> 00:03:00.833
that his mind becomes unstable.

15
00:03:00.833 --> 00:03:02.291
Arjun then sees

16
00:03:02.291 --> 00:03:04.541
what is about to happen to the warriors.

17
00:03:04.541 --> 00:03:06.166
What is their fate?

18
00:03:06.166 --> 00:03:09.291
Bhishma, Drona, Karna, and countless

19
00:03:09.291 --> 00:03:11.291
soldiers are rushing into Lord Krishna's

20
00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.375
fiery mouths.

21
00:03:13.375 --> 00:03:16.750
Some of their heads crushed between His teeth.

22
00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:18.791
He understands that Lord Krishna

23
00:03:18.791 --> 00:03:20.666
is showing him the future.

24
00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:24.333
That unavoidable destruction

25
00:03:24.333 --> 00:03:27.041
which the war will bring.

26
00:03:32.041 --> 00:03:33.291
Arjun's fear

27
00:03:33.291 --> 00:03:35.125
grows further

28
00:03:35.125 --> 00:03:36.458
as he describes

29
00:03:36.458 --> 00:03:38.416
what he is seeing.

30
00:03:38.416 --> 00:03:39.875
The all-pervading Vishnu

31
00:03:39.875 --> 00:03:42.625
is no longer merely a source of wonder.

32
00:03:42.625 --> 00:03:46.708
His vast form touching the sky,
His shining colours,

33
00:03:46.708 --> 00:03:50.333
and His fiery eyes are overwhelming.

34
00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:51.666
Arjun loses control

35
00:03:51.666 --> 00:03:54.708
over his thoughts and emotions,

36
00:03:54.708 --> 00:03:57.583
becoming unable to remain calm.

37
00:03:57.583 --> 00:04:00.333
As he looks deeper,

38
00:04:00.333 --> 00:04:03.166
he begins to beg for mercy.

39
00:04:03.166 --> 00:04:06.166
He sees Lord Krishna's terrifying, blazing mouths

40
00:04:06.166 --> 00:04:08.125
and enormous teeth,

41
00:04:08.125 --> 00:04:11.500
which seem like the fire of cosmic destruction.

42
00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.000
The fear is so intense

43
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.000
that Arjun loses his sense of direction.

44
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.750
He cannot even tell where he is.

45
00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.833
Then the most terrifying part appears.

46
00:04:22.833 --> 00:04:24.750
Arjun sees the warriors of both armies

47
00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.708
being swallowed by the Vishwarupa.

48
00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:28.166
Not only

49
00:04:28.166 --> 00:04:31.166
Duryodhan and his brothers,
but Bhishma, Drona,

50
00:04:31.166 --> 00:04:32.333
and Karna too.

51
00:04:32.333 --> 00:04:34.166
Some of the greatest warriors

52
00:04:34.166 --> 00:04:38.000
of the battlefield are rushing
into Lord Krishna's mouths.

53
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.083
He sees some of them

54
00:04:39.083 --> 00:04:41.541
with their heads crushed

55
00:04:41.541 --> 00:04:44.166
between Lord Krishna's teeth.

56
00:04:44.166 --> 00:04:47.125
At this point, Arjun understands that Lord

57
00:04:47.125 --> 00:04:49.333
Krishna is showing him the future.

58
00:04:49.333 --> 00:04:51.708
In the previous verses, Lord Krishna had said

59
00:04:51.708 --> 00:04:52.583
that Arjun

60
00:04:52.583 --> 00:04:56.333
could see whatever he wished,
including the future.

61
00:04:56.333 --> 00:05:00.083
Now Arjun sees it appearing before his eyes.

62
00:05:00.083 --> 00:05:03.375
The great warriors of the war will be destroyed,

63
00:05:03.375 --> 00:05:06.208
whatever the outcome of the battle.

64
00:05:06.208 --> 00:05:08.291
To describe this destruction,

65
00:05:08.291 --> 00:05:10.916
Arjun gives two powerful examples.

66
00:05:10.916 --> 00:05:12.291
First,

67
00:05:12.291 --> 00:05:14.833
rivers flowing into the ocean.

68
00:05:14.833 --> 00:05:16.541
This represents warriors

69
00:05:16.541 --> 00:05:20.000
like Bhishma and Drona,

70
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.416
who are naturally

71
00:05:21.416 --> 00:05:24.000
flowing toward their destiny,

72
00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.291
without any hostility.

73
00:05:26.291 --> 00:05:29.125
They are simply following the higher plan

74
00:05:29.125 --> 00:05:32.750
set by the divine order.

75
00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:36.416
Second, moths rushing into a fire,

76
00:05:36.416 --> 00:05:38.958
or warriors like Karna, Shakuni, and Duryodhan,

77
00:05:38.958 --> 00:05:42.000
whom this represents,

78
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:45.916
who, through their ego and wrong and Drona,

79
00:05:45.916 --> 00:05:49.375
actively choosing their own destruction.

80
00:05:49.375 --> 00:05:52.166
They are not merely being carried by fate.

81
00:05:52.166 --> 00:05:55.500
They are running toward their
own ruin themselves.

82
00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:56.375
Arjun

83
00:05:56.375 --> 00:05:58.166
then sees with fear

84
00:05:58.166 --> 00:06:00.083
that Lord Krishna's vast, fiery,

85
00:06:00.083 --> 00:06:01.333
blazing mouths

86
00:06:01.333 --> 00:06:04.250
are consuming everyone from all directions.

87
00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:07.000
His radiance covers the universe,

88
00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.500
and His scorching

89
00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.458
rays burn everything.

90
00:06:11.458 --> 00:06:14.041
No one is spared from this form.

91
00:06:14.041 --> 00:06:15.958
Lord Krishna Himself is time,

92
00:06:15.958 --> 00:06:18.416
which spares no one.

93
00:06:18.416 --> 00:06:19.708
At this point, Arjun

94
00:06:19.708 --> 00:06:22.250
grasps a deep truth.

95
00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:24.625
Destruction is not separate from Lord Krishna.

96
00:06:24.625 --> 00:06:28.500
It too is part of the divine reality.

97
00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.916
Just as creation and sustenance
are aspects of the Lord,

98
00:06:31.916 --> 00:06:35.125
in the same way, dissolution is also one aspect.

99
00:06:35.125 --> 00:06:36.708
The Vishwarupa shows

100
00:06:36.708 --> 00:06:40.375
that in the material world
everything is temporary.

101
00:06:40.375 --> 00:06:43.041
There is a great teaching in this realisation.

102
00:06:43.041 --> 00:06:46.666
If we attach our mind to the temporary world,

103
00:06:46.666 --> 00:06:50.250
then when it is taken away, we suffer.

104
00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:53.125
But if we fix our love and devotion

105
00:06:53.125 --> 00:06:54.291
on Lord Krishna,

106
00:06:54.291 --> 00:06:56.416
the eternal,

107
00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:57.125
then we rise above

108
00:06:57.125 --> 00:07:00.291
the cycle of birth and death.

109
00:07:00.291 --> 00:07:02.666
Through this vision, Lord Krishna

110
00:07:02.666 --> 00:07:05.666
is teaching Arjun and all of us

111
00:07:05.666 --> 00:07:08.750
that the only true shelter is in Him.

112
00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:10.375
Everything else, however

113
00:07:10.375 --> 00:07:13.208
powerful or grand,

114
00:07:13.208 --> 00:07:15.666
is bound to perish.

115
00:07:15.666 --> 00:07:17.083
The only thing

116
00:07:17.083 --> 00:07:20.250
that remains beyond time and destruction

117
00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:23.250
is devotion to the Supreme Lord.

118
00:07:27.791 --> 00:07:30.416
Think.

119
00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:34.583
Since death is certain,

120
00:07:34.583 --> 00:07:38.666
is it right to be afraid of it,

121
00:07:38.666 --> 00:07:43.375
or is it right to accept it as an inevitable truth

122
00:07:43.375 --> 00:07:48.416
and prepare to make it
a meaningful, fulfilling passage?

123
00:07:48.416 --> 00:07:52.500
Which is right?

124
00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.916
Death is certain for all,

125
00:07:55.916 --> 00:07:59.875
but how you live,

126
00:07:59.875 --> 00:08:04.500
from this alone all the difference arises.

127
00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.750
Try to remember

128
00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.041
old acquaintances

129
00:08:09.041 --> 00:08:13.541
who were friendly and good-natured.

130
00:08:13.541 --> 00:08:17.666
Their memory gives you joy,

131
00:08:17.666 --> 00:08:20.625
and those who were selfish,

132
00:08:20.625 --> 00:08:25.083
their memories fill you with bitterness,

133
00:08:25.083 --> 00:08:30.208
however successful they may
have been in their professional life.

134
00:08:30.208 --> 00:08:32.250
Given the chance,

135
00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:35.125
you would want to honour the friendly

136
00:08:35.125 --> 00:08:37.791
acquaintances,

137
00:08:37.791 --> 00:08:39.875
not the selfish ones.

138
00:08:39.875 --> 00:08:42.458
In My Vishwarupa,

139
00:08:42.458 --> 00:08:46.166
the two paths Arjun saw,

140
00:08:46.166 --> 00:08:49.041
pay attention to them.

141
00:08:49.041 --> 00:08:50.666
Those who

142
00:08:50.666 --> 00:08:53.041
live with dharma,

143
00:08:53.041 --> 00:08:57.750
with honesty, kindness, and duty,

144
00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:00.458
are like the rivers

145
00:09:00.458 --> 00:09:03.500
that flow toward the ocean.

146
00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:04.875
They move

147
00:09:04.875 --> 00:09:09.083
toward life's end naturally

148
00:09:09.083 --> 00:09:11.833
and peacefully.

149
00:09:11.833 --> 00:09:16.041
Nourishing others along the way,

150
00:09:16.041 --> 00:09:17.708
their presence

151
00:09:17.708 --> 00:09:22.041
lifts up the people around them,

152
00:09:22.041 --> 00:09:26.541
leaving behind a legacy of goodness and love.

153
00:09:26.541 --> 00:09:28.500
On the other hand,

154
00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:32.458
those who live selfishly, chasing power,

155
00:09:32.458 --> 00:09:36.625
greed, and ego,

156
00:09:36.625 --> 00:09:39.500
are like the moths

157
00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:43.250
that rush toward the fire.

158
00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:45.625
Their choices bring sorrow

159
00:09:45.625 --> 00:09:46.750
not only

160
00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:51.083
for themselves, but also for those people

161
00:09:51.083 --> 00:09:56.125
whom they harm along the way.

162
00:09:56.125 --> 00:09:58.791
They are consumed quickly

163
00:09:58.791 --> 00:10:01.666
and leave behind regret

164
00:10:01.666 --> 00:10:04.833
and sorrow.

165
00:10:04.833 --> 00:10:06.916
So ask yourself,

166
00:10:06.916 --> 00:10:11.208
are you living like a river?

167
00:10:11.208 --> 00:10:13.250
Giving others comfort,

168
00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:16.458
knowledge, and support,

169
00:10:16.458 --> 00:10:22.166
or are you, like a moth, running toward destruction 

170
00:10:22.166 --> 00:10:24.833
harming yourself

171
00:10:24.833 --> 00:10:26.750
and the people

172
00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:30.458
around you?

173
00:10:30.458 --> 00:10:32.708
Choose the path of dharma.

174
00:10:32.708 --> 00:10:36.000
Your life will flow with meaning, peace,

175
00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:39.291
and lasting impact.

176
00:10:43.958 --> 00:10:46.541
In family life,

177
00:10:46.541 --> 00:10:49.500
speaking openly about death

178
00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.875
is important.

179
00:10:51.875 --> 00:10:55.000
Not as something to fear,

180
00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.666
but

181
00:10:56.666 --> 00:11:00.958
as a natural part of life.

182
00:11:00.958 --> 00:11:03.875
Just as Arjun saw the warriors

183
00:11:03.875 --> 00:11:07.916
flowing toward their end,

184
00:11:07.916 --> 00:11:10.916
everyone's journey ultimately

185
00:11:10.916 --> 00:11:14.375
reaches its destination.

186
00:11:14.375 --> 00:11:17.125
Accepting this truth

187
00:11:17.125 --> 00:11:20.958
makes you more responsible, humble,

188
00:11:20.958 --> 00:11:23.833
and focused on what truly

189
00:11:23.833 --> 00:11:25.791
matters.

190
00:11:25.791 --> 00:11:30.291
Suppose, in some social organisation,

191
00:11:30.291 --> 00:11:33.250
a high position is to be obtained,

192
00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:34.833
and for it

193
00:11:34.833 --> 00:11:39.750
deception is said to be necessary.

194
00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:42.291
Then consider.

195
00:11:42.291 --> 00:11:45.958
What is the benefit of obtaining such a position

196
00:11:45.958 --> 00:11:51.416
whose very foundation is flawed?

197
00:11:51.416 --> 00:11:52.375
This position's

198
00:11:52.375 --> 00:11:57.000
term will end one day,

199
00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:03.500
but its dishonour will stay attached forever.

200
00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:05.250
Even without a position,

201
00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:08.541
social service can be done,

202
00:12:08.541 --> 00:12:13.583
which will make your name immortal forever.

203
00:12:13.583 --> 00:12:18.458
When you understand that life is temporary,

204
00:12:18.458 --> 00:12:21.500
then in your choices

205
00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:25.166
you become more thoughtful.

206
00:12:25.166 --> 00:12:26.666
Temptation

207
00:12:26.666 --> 00:12:30.708
and distraction cannot influence you,

208
00:12:30.708 --> 00:12:32.541
because you know

209
00:12:32.541 --> 00:12:36.833
that they lead nowhere.

210
00:12:36.833 --> 00:12:38.583
Instead,

211
00:12:38.583 --> 00:12:41.250
you focus on living with kindness,

212
00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:42.750
honesty,

213
00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:46.041
and purpose.

214
00:12:46.041 --> 00:12:47.125
This awareness

215
00:12:47.125 --> 00:12:51.000
helps you stay calm during life's ups

216
00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:54.250
and downs.

217
00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:58.166
Knowing that everything

218
00:12:58.208 --> 00:13:00.958
is part of a larger plan,

219
00:13:00.958 --> 00:13:04.125
teach your family

220
00:13:04.125 --> 00:13:06.416
that living with dharma,

221
00:13:06.416 --> 00:13:11.708
doing what is right, leaves a lasting impact.

222
00:13:11.708 --> 00:13:13.583
Just as a river

223
00:13:13.583 --> 00:13:15.833
goes along its path

224
00:13:15.833 --> 00:13:19.791
nourishing everyone,

225
00:13:19.791 --> 00:13:24.875
in the same way, a life lived with virtues

226
00:13:24.875 --> 00:13:27.041
brings peace

227
00:13:27.041 --> 00:13:30.291
and happiness for others.

228
00:13:30.291 --> 00:13:32.333
Reflecting on death

229
00:13:32.333 --> 00:13:35.250
does not limit life.

230
00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:40.000
It makes every moment more meaningful

231
00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.583
and every choice more

232
00:13:42.583 --> 00:13:45.083
purposeful.

233
00:13:49.791 --> 00:13:52.791
Reflect calmly on this.

234
00:13:52.791 --> 00:13:57.625
When you were not there,
creation was still running.

235
00:13:57.625 --> 00:14:01.500
After you too, it will keep running.

236
00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:04.125
In that case, to consider yourself

237
00:14:04.125 --> 00:14:08.416
entirely the cause of any event,

238
00:14:08.416 --> 00:14:11.250
how right is that?

239
00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:15.541
In your professional life, it is easy to believe

240
00:14:15.541 --> 00:14:19.333
that success or failure depends entirely

241
00:14:19.333 --> 00:14:23.541
on your efforts.

242
00:14:23.541 --> 00:14:26.250
But true wisdom comes

243
00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:29.958
when you let go of the mindset of 

244
00:14:29.958 --> 00:14:35.125
considering yourself the only doer.

245
00:14:35.125 --> 00:14:36.750
Just as Arjun

246
00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:38.875
saw the destruction of the warriors

247
00:14:38.875 --> 00:14:41.625
as part of a larger plan

248
00:14:41.625 --> 00:14:46.000
beyond his own control,

249
00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:48.416
you too must understand

250
00:14:48.416 --> 00:14:52.208
that although your actions are important,

251
00:14:52.208 --> 00:14:54.625
but the outcomes,

252
00:14:54.625 --> 00:14:57.833
the outcomes are not always in your hands.

253
00:14:57.833 --> 00:15:00.625
Your role is, with focus

254
00:15:00.625 --> 00:15:02.208
and dedication,

255
00:15:02.208 --> 00:15:05.291
to give your very best.

256
00:15:05.291 --> 00:15:08.541
Without attachment to results,

257
00:15:08.541 --> 00:15:09.750
when you

258
00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:13.333
cling too tightly to the idea of success

259
00:15:13.333 --> 00:15:16.083
or fear failure,

260
00:15:16.083 --> 00:15:19.250
then stress and anxiety arise.

261
00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:22.250
But when you experience

262
00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:25.583
that outcomes, beyond your control,

263
00:15:25.583 --> 00:15:26.541
by many other

264
00:15:26.541 --> 00:15:30.291
causes too are determined,

265
00:15:30.291 --> 00:15:34.916
then you find freedom
from unnecessary pressure.

266
00:15:34.916 --> 00:15:37.541
Work with excellence,

267
00:15:37.541 --> 00:15:43.416
but let go the need to control every outcome.

268
00:15:43.416 --> 00:15:46.708
This mindset not only brings peace,

269
00:15:46.708 --> 00:15:50.416
but also makes you more confident

270
00:15:50.416 --> 00:15:53.708
and resilient.

271
00:15:53.708 --> 00:15:58.041
Success becomes a celebration of your effort,

272
00:15:58.041 --> 00:16:00.000
and failures

273
00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:03.750
become lessons without regret.

274
00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:08.041
You just do your work with a sincere heart.

275
00:16:08.041 --> 00:16:10.125
Leave to Me

276
00:16:10.125 --> 00:16:12.000
all the results.
